  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience and adapting to climate change in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aims to strengthen the resilience of poor households in Malawi to withstand current and projected weather and climate-related shocks and stresses. This will in turn halt the annual cycle of humanitarian crises that blights people&#x2019;s lives, harms poverty reduction efforts and swallows up resources. The UK will invest up to &#xa3;90.5 million over eight years [2018-2027] to provide direct benefits to 1.7 million poor and vulnerable people in Malawi [approximately 300,000 households].The programme also supports environmental and resilience outcomes through reducing deforestation directly and indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
